# Trivy ignore list for the sidecar image (PENG-5554). Used by deploy.yaml,
# image-scan.yml and the wrapper repo's weekly scan of the deployed image.
# Add an entry only when no fixed version exists, with a reason and a review
# date; remove it once a fix lands. Re-check the whole list on every
# golden-image or upstream bump.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Day-one entries (2026-11-23). Every one is in the Bark golden base image
# (ghcr.io/bark-com/python:<ver>-alpine-3.22.4-nonroot), not in this repo's
# code or its uv.lock. They are fixed by a golden-image rebuild, which arrives
# here as a golden-image-update PR; golden-images v1 builds were last green on
# 2026-11-04. REVIEW BY 2026-12-07: on every golden-image bump, rerun Trivy
# with this file emptied and delete each entry that no longer reports.

# --- Alpine `python3` placeholder package (false positives) -----------------
# The golden image registers a virtual apk package `python3` versioned "3.12"
# so apk does not pull the system Python; the real interpreter is the golden
# build in /usr/local. Trivy matches the placeholder against old Alpine python3
# advisories (fixed versions like 3.6.8-r1 are lower than "3.12"). Not code
# that exists in the image.
